note top of MediaLibraryScanningService
  Central service that resolves the scanner of the library type,
  builds the scan job graph, registers the scan in the cancellation
  and progress trackers, and publishes the scan started events.
  It returns the file system discovery job, which is the root of
  the graph and whose execution completes the entire scan.
end note

' ============================== QUEUE AND PROCESSING ==============================

interface IMediaLibrariesScanQueue {
    + Writer: ChannelWriter<MediaLibraryScanCompositeId>
    + Reader: ChannelReader<MediaLibraryScanCompositeId>
}

class MediaLibrariesScanQueue {
    - _channel: Channel<MediaLibraryScanCompositeId>
    + Writer: ChannelWriter<MediaLibraryScanCompositeId>
    + Reader: ChannelReader<MediaLibraryScanCompositeId>
}

note bottom of MediaLibrariesScanQueue
  In-memory queue of scan composite ids. The scan processor
  prepares and executes one scan at a time, so the scans run
  consecutively, in the order in which they were queued. The
  jobs of a scan are never placed on this queue.
end note

class MediaLibraryScanProcessorJob {
    - _mediaLibrariesScanQueue: IMediaLibrariesScanQueue
    - _mediaLibrariesScanCancellationTracker: IMediaLibrariesScanCancellationTracker
    - _serviceScopeFactory: IServiceScopeFactory
    - _logger: ILogger<MediaLibraryScanProcessorJob>
    # ExecuteAsync(token: CancellationToken): Task
    - ProcessScanAsync(compositeId: MediaLibraryScanCompositeId, token: CancellationToken): Task
    - ReportScanFailureAsync(compositeId: MediaLibraryScanCompositeId, libraryId: LibraryId, exception: Exception, token: CancellationToken): Task
}

note top of MediaLibraryScanProcessorJob
  Background service that consumes the queued scan ids one at a
  time, reads the pending scan, prepares its job graph through the
  scanning service and executes the discovery job. A failing scan
  is reported and does not stop the scans queued behind it.
end note

